menu "WS2812B Clock Wifi"

    config WIFI_SSID
        string "Wifi SSID"
        default ""
        help
            Wifi SSID

    config WIFI_PSK
        string "Wifi Password"
        default ""
        help
            Wiffi Passphrase / Pre-Shared Key

    config WIFI_MAXIMUM_RETRY
        int "Maximum retry"
        default 5
        help
            Set the Maximum retry to avoid station reconnecting to the AP unlimited when the AP is really inexistent.

    config WIFI_POWER_SAVE
        bool "WiFi power save (modem sleep)"
        default n
        help
            Let the radio sleep between the access point's DTIM beacons. This
            is ESP-IDF's default for a station, and it costs throughput and
            latency: at a DTIM period of 3 the radio wakes roughly every
            300 ms, which was measured turning an 850 KB OTA download into a
            four minute one and putting ping times at 140-430 ms on a LAN.

            A mains-powered clock has nothing to gain from it, so it is off
            here. Turn it on for a battery-powered build.

endmenu
